<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>No magnetic field ASR</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We distinguish a teacher model <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>, which induces the ground-truth hierarchical decomposition of configurations, from a student model <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{W},\hat{\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{W},\hat{\beta})</annotation></semantics></math>, which generates predictions by sampling.
Given an input <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, define the teacher and student couplings</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{T}(x):=J(x,W),\qquad J_{S}(x):=J(x,\hat{W})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{T}(x):=J(x,W),\qquad J_{S}(x):=J(x,\hat{W}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Fix a level <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in\{1,\dots,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in\{1,\dots,L\}</annotation></semantics></math>. A (size-biased) ordering of level-<math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> clusters
<math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{r}(J_{T}(x))\}_{r\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{r}(J_{T}(x))\}_{r\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in Section <a href="#S1" title="1 Introduction ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Let the corresponding teacher Gibbs weights be</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W^{(l)}_{r}(x)\;:=\;S_{\beta}\!\big(\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{r}(J_{T}(x));\,J_{T}(x)\big),\qquad r=1,2,\dots," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{(l)}_{r}(x)\;:=\;S_{\beta}\!\big(\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{r}(J_{T}(x));\,J_{T}(x)\big),\qquad r=1,2,\dots,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">so that <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{r\geq 1}W^{(l)}_{r}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{r\geq 1}W^{(l)}_{r}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. In the <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> limit, the random sequence <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W^{(l)}_{r}(x)\}_{r\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W^{(l)}_{r}(x)\}_{r\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> is described
by a Poisson–Dirichlet <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{m_{l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{m_{l}}</annotation></semantics></math> / stick-breaking construction with parameter <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{l}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{l}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{i}^{(l)}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{indep.}}}{{\sim}}\mathrm{Beta}(1-m_{l},\,im_{l}),\qquad i=1,2,\dots," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mover><mo>∼</mo><mtext>indep.</mtext></mover><mi>Beta</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}^{(l)}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{indep.}}}{{\sim}}\mathrm{Beta}(1-m_{l},\,im_{l}),\qquad i=1,2,\dots,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">with</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{(l)}_{1}=V^{(l)}_{1},\qquad W^{(l)}_{i}=V^{(l)}_{i}\prod_{j&lt;i}(1-V^{(l)}_{j}),\quad i\geq 2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{(l)}_{1}=V^{(l)}_{1},\qquad W^{(l)}_{i}=V^{(l)}_{i}\prod_{j&lt;i}(1-V^{(l)}_{j}),\quad i\geq 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">The parameter <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is determined from the probability density <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> of the overlap of two randomly chosen configurations <math id="A1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma,\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma,\tau</annotation></semantics></math> as follows<span id="footnote7" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">7</span>
            
            
            
          In particular the probability of leaves at the final level is distributed as <math id="footnote7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{m_{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{m_{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="footnote7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{L}=1-\mu(q_{L+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{L}=1-\mu(q_{L+1})</annotation></semantics></math> (Theorem 15.4.4 in M. Talagrand Vol. II).</span></span></span></p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E22X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu(R(\sigma,\tau)=q_{l})=m_{l}-m_{l-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu(R(\sigma,\tau)=q_{l})=m_{l}-m_{l-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">This gives the natural ordering</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}:=0&lt;m_{1}&lt;m_{2}&lt;\dots&lt;m_{L}&lt;m_{L+1}:=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}:=0&lt;m_{1}&lt;m_{2}&lt;\dots&lt;m_{L}&lt;m_{L+1}:=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we analyze inference-time gains in the matched setting <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{W}=W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{W}=W</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{T}=J_{S}=J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{T}=J_{S}=J</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\beta}=\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\beta}=\beta</annotation></semantics></math>
so that a single prediction <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma\sim p_{\hat{\beta}}(\cdot\mid J(x,W))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\sim p_{\hat{\beta}}(\cdot\mid J(x,W))</annotation></semantics></math> lands in the
teacher cluster <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{r}(J(x,W))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{r}(J(x,W))</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{(l)}_{r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{(l)}_{r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall the teacher correct set at level <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> is the union of the first <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> clusters</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J(x,W)):=\bigcup_{r=1}^{m}\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{r}(J(x,W))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J(x,W)):=\bigcup_{r=1}^{m}\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{r}(J(x,W)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In the matched setting, the probability that a single try is safe (i.e., does not land in
<math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J_{T}(x,W))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J_{T}(x,W))</annotation></semantics></math>) is the residual mass</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{l,m}\;=\;1-\sum_{i=1}^{m}W^{(l)}_{i}\;=\;\prod_{i=1}^{m}(1-V^{(l)}_{i})\;=\;\prod_{i=1}^{m}U_{i},\qquad U_{i}:=1-V^{(l)}_{i}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(im_{l},\,1-m_{l})\ \text{independent.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>independent.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{l,m}\;=\;1-\sum_{i=1}^{m}W^{(l)}_{i}\;=\;\prod_{i=1}^{m}(1-V^{(l)}_{i})\;=\;\prod_{i=1}^{m}U_{i},\qquad U_{i}:=1-V^{(l)}_{i}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(im_{l},\,1-m_{l})\ \text{independent.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> independent attempts, the attack success rate/probability (ASR) is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{k}\;:=\;1-p_{l,m}^{k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{k}\;:=\;1-p_{l,m}^{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">i.e., the probability that at least one attempt lands in <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J(x,W))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J(x,W))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To the leading order in large <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big[\Pi_{k}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big[\Pi_{k}\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(im_{l}+k)\,\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(im_{l})\,\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}+k\big)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.584em;" width="0.584em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.584em;" width="0.584em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(im_{l}+k)\,\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(im_{l})\,\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}+k\big)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Exact)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big[\Pi_{k}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big[\Pi_{k}\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-C_{m}(m_{l})\,k^{-m(1-m_{l})}\!\left(1-\frac{m_{l}(1-m_{l})m^{2}}{2k}+O(k^{-2})\right),\qquad k\to\infty," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-C_{m}(m_{l})\,k^{-m(1-m_{l})}\!\left(1-\frac{m_{l}(1-m_{l})m^{2}}{2k}+O(k^{-2})\right),\qquad k\to\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Asymptotic)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{m}(m_{l})\;=\;\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(im_{l})}\;=\;\frac{\Gamma(1)\Gamma(1+m_{l})\cdots\Gamma\!\big(1+(m-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(m_{l})\Gamma(2m_{l})\cdots\Gamma(mm_{l})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.584em;" width="0.584em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mpadded style="width:0.584em;" width="0.584em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mpadded><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{m}(m_{l})\;=\;\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(im_{l})}\;=\;\frac{\Gamma(1)\Gamma(1+m_{l})\cdots\Gamma\!\big(1+(m-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(m_{l})\Gamma(2m_{l})\cdots\Gamma(mm_{l})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, the <em id="Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">gap to certainty</em> decays polynomially:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\mathbb{E}[\Pi_{k}]\asymp k^{-\,\nu},\qquad\nu=m(1-m_{l})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\mathbb{E}[\Pi_{k}]\asymp k^{-\,\nu},\qquad\nu=m(1-m_{l}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the stick-breaking construction with parameter <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{l}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{l}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the residual mass after <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> breaks is
<math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{l,m}=\prod_{i=1}^{m}(1-V^{(l)}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{l,m}=\prod_{i=1}^{m}(1-V^{(l)}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{(l)}_{i}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(1-m_{l},\,im_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{(l)}_{i}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(1-m_{l},\,im_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> independent.
Setting <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}:=1-V^{(l)}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}:=1-V^{(l)}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(im_{l},\,1-m_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(im_{l},\,1-m_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> (again independent) and hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{l,m}=\prod_{i=1}^{m}U_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{l,m}=\prod_{i=1}^{m}U_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\sim\mathrm{Beta}(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\sim\mathrm{Beta}(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th moment is
<math id="A1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[U^{k}]=\frac{\Gamma(a+k)\Gamma(a+b)}{\Gamma(a)\Gamma(a+b+k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[U^{k}]=\frac{\Gamma(a+k)\Gamma(a+b)}{\Gamma(a)\Gamma(a+b+k)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Independence gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{l,m}^{\,k}\right]=\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(im_{l}+k)\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(im_{l})\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}+k\big)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.584em;" width="0.584em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.584em;" width="0.584em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{l,m}^{\,k}\right]=\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(im_{l}+k)\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(im_{l})\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}+k\big)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore <math id="A1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Pi_{k}]=1-\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{\,k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Pi_{k}]=1-\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{\,k}]</annotation></semantics></math> and equation <a href="#A1.Ex10" title="In Result 3. ‣ Appendix A No magnetic field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Exact</span></a> follows.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Use the standard gamma-ratio expansion</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Gamma(k+a)}{\Gamma(k+b)}=k^{a-b}\!\left(1+\frac{(a-b)(a+b-1)}{2k}+O(k^{-2})\right),\qquad k\to\infty," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Gamma(k+a)}{\Gamma(k+b)}=k^{a-b}\!\left(1+\frac{(a-b)(a+b-1)}{2k}+O(k^{-2})\right),\qquad k\to\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">valid for fixed <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th factor in <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{\,k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{\,k}]</annotation></semantics></math> one has <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=im_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=im_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=1+(i-1)m_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=1+(i-1)m_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a-b=m_{l}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a-b=m_{l}-1</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b-1=(2i-1)m_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b-1=(2i-1)m_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>. Multiplying the <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> factors yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{l,m}^{\,k}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[p_{l,m}^{\,k}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(im_{l})}\right)k^{\sum_{i=1}^{m}(m_{l}-1)}\left(1-\frac{m_{l}(1-m_{l})}{2k}\sum_{i=1}^{m}(2i-1)+O(k^{-2})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.584em;" width="0.584em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(im_{l})}\right)k^{\sum_{i=1}^{m}(m_{l}-1)}\left(1-\frac{m_{l}(1-m_{l})}{2k}\sum_{i=1}^{m}(2i-1)+O(k^{-2})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{m}(m_{l})\,k^{-m(1-m_{l})}\left(1-\frac{m_{l}(1-m_{l})}{2k}\,m^{2}+O(k^{-2})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{m}(m_{l})\,k^{-m(1-m_{l})}\left(1-\frac{m_{l}(1-m_{l})}{2k}\,m^{2}+O(k^{-2})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">because <math id="A1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{m}(2i-1)=m^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{m}(2i-1)=m^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting into <math id="A1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Pi_{k}]=1-\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{\,k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Pi_{k}]=1-\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{\,k}]</annotation></semantics></math>
gives equation <a href="#A1.Ex11" title="In Result 3. ‣ Appendix A No magnetic field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Asymptotic</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Weak field ASR</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We call a student draw <em id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">correct</em> (or <em id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">successful</em>) if it lands in the union of the teacher’s first <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> level-<math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> clusters. The cluster-level accuracy is</p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{N}(h)\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{J}\Big[\ \mathbb{P}_{\sigma\sim p^{(h)}_{\beta}(\cdot\mid J)}\big(\sigma\in\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J)\big)\ \Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">[</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{N}(h)\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{J}\Big[\ \mathbb{P}_{\sigma\sim p^{(h)}_{\beta}(\cdot\mid J)}\big(\sigma\in\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J)\big)\ \Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">At level <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> we use overlap separation. For <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{i}(J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{i}(J)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\sigma,\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{i}(J))\approx q_{l+1},\quad R(\sigma,\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{j}(J))\lesssim q_{l}\text{ for }j\neq i," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\sigma,\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{i}(J))\approx q_{l+1},\quad R(\sigma,\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{j}(J))\lesssim q_{l}\text{ for }j\neq i,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">while for <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\notin\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\notin\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\sigma,\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{i}(J))\lesssim q_{l}\text{ for all }i\in\{1,\ldots,m\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\sigma,\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{i}(J))\lesssim q_{l}\text{ for all }i\in\{1,\ldots,m\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The magnetic field contribution to the energy for a configuration <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{i}(J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\mathcal{C}^{(l)}_{i}(J)</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>) is:</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta E_{\text{mag}}(\sigma)=-h\sum_{j=1}^{N}\sigma_{j}\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{i}(J)_{j}-h\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}j^{\prime}=1\\
j^{\prime}\neq i\end{subarray}}^{m}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\sigma_{k}\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{j^{\prime}}(J)_{k}\approx-hNq_{l+1}-hN(m-1)q_{l}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>mag</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>h</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mi>m</mi></munderover><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">≈</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta E_{\text{mag}}(\sigma)=-h\sum_{j=1}^{N}\sigma_{j}\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{i}(J)_{j}-h\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}j^{\prime}=1\\
j^{\prime}\neq i\end{subarray}}^{m}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\sigma_{k}\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{j^{\prime}}(J)_{k}\approx-hNq_{l+1}-hN(m-1)q_{l},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the second term is negligible due to cluster orthogonality. For <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\notin\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\notin\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J)</annotation></semantics></math>, the energy shift is approximately <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-hNmq_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-hNmq_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This implies the magnetic field reweights the aggregate probability mass of the first <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> clusters (the unsafe region <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}:=\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}:=\mathcal{T}^{(l)}_{m}(J)</annotation></semantics></math>) relative to
its complement by a factor <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\;:=\;\beta hN\Delta_{q},\quad\Delta_{q}:=q_{l+1}-q_{l}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\;:=\;\beta hN\Delta_{q},\quad\Delta_{q}:=q_{l+1}-q_{l}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{m}^{(\text{total})}:=\sum_{i=1}^{m}W^{(l)}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{m}^{(\text{total})}:=\sum_{i=1}^{m}W^{(l)}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the aggregate teacher mass in the first <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> clusters, and <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{l,m}:=1-W_{m}^{(\text{total})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{l,m}:=1-W_{m}^{(\text{total})}</annotation></semantics></math> the residual mass. Conditioning on <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{m}^{(\text{total})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{m}^{(\text{total})}</annotation></semantics></math>, the student’s single-draw
success probability is approximated by<span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
            
            
            
          This idea is motivated by the recent paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aguilar-Janita et al. (2024)</a></cite>.</span></span></span></p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{N}(h\mid W_{m}^{(\text{total})})\;\approx\;\frac{W_{m}^{(\text{total})}e^{\lambda}}{(1-W_{m}^{(\text{total})})+W_{m}^{(\text{total})}e^{\lambda}}\;=\;\frac{W_{m}^{(\text{total})}e^{\lambda}}{p_{l,m}+W_{m}^{(\text{total})}e^{\lambda}}\;=\;1-\frac{p_{l,m}}{p_{l,m}+(1-p_{l,m})e^{\lambda}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{N}(h\mid W_{m}^{(\text{total})})\;\approx\;\frac{W_{m}^{(\text{total})}e^{\lambda}}{(1-W_{m}^{(\text{total})})+W_{m}^{(\text{total})}e^{\lambda}}\;=\;\frac{W_{m}^{(\text{total})}e^{\lambda}}{p_{l,m}+W_{m}^{(\text{total})}e^{\lambda}}\;=\;1-\frac{p_{l,m}}{p_{l,m}+(1-p_{l,m})e^{\lambda}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Averaging over <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to sampling <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{m}^{(\text{total})}=1-p_{l,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{m}^{(\text{total})}=1-p_{l,m}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{l,m}=\prod_{i=1}^{m}U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{l,m}=\prod_{i=1}^{m}U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}\sim\text{Beta}(im_{l},1-m_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}\sim\text{Beta}(im_{l},1-m_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> are independent.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To the leading order in large <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-sample attack success rate satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\Pi_{k}(N,h)=\frac{1}{e^{k\lambda}}\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\binom{k+n-1}{n}\alpha^{n}\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{k+n}],\quad\alpha=1-e^{-\lambda}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\Pi_{k}(N,h)=\frac{1}{e^{k\lambda}}\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\binom{k+n-1}{n}\alpha^{n}\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{k+n}],\quad\alpha=1-e^{-\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With</span></p>
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E29X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\left(\prod_{j=1}^{m}u_{j}\right)^{k}\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(1+(i-1)m_{l})}{\Gamma(im_{l})\Gamma(1-m_{l})}u_{i}^{im_{l}-1}(1-u_{i})^{-m_{l}}\,du_{1}\cdots du_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\left(\prod_{j=1}^{m}u_{j}\right)^{k}\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(1+(i-1)m_{l})}{\Gamma(im_{l})\Gamma(1-m_{l})}u_{i}^{im_{l}-1}(1-u_{i})^{-m_{l}}\,du_{1}\cdots du_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E29Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(im_{l}+k)\Gamma(1+(i-1)m_{l})}{\Gamma(1+(i-1)m_{l}+k)\Gamma(im_{l})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(im_{l}+k)\Gamma(1+(i-1)m_{l})}{\Gamma(1+(i-1)m_{l}+k)\Gamma(im_{l})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the joint limit <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> with the scaling variable
<math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:=k\lambda^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:=k\lambda^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
held <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E30X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1-\Pi_{k}(N,h)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1-\Pi_{k}(N,h)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{m}(m_{l})\,k^{-\nu}\,e^{-\frac{g}{2}}\bigg[(1+\frac{g}{2}+O(g^{2}))+\frac{1}{\sqrt{k}}\,(-\nu\,\sqrt{g}+O(g^{3/2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ν</mi><msqrt><mi>g</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{m}(m_{l})\,k^{-\nu}\,e^{-\frac{g}{2}}\bigg[(1+\frac{g}{2}+O(g^{2}))+\frac{1}{\sqrt{k}}\,(-\nu\,\sqrt{g}+O(g^{3/2}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E30Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{k}\,(-a+O(g))+O\!\left(\frac{1}{k\sqrt{k}}\right)\bigg]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{k}\,(-a+O(g))+O\!\left(\frac{1}{k\sqrt{k}}\right)\bigg],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=m(1-m_{l}),\quad a=\frac{m_{l}(1-m_{l})m^{2}}{2},\quad C_{m}(m_{l})\;=\;\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(im_{l})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.584em;" width="0.584em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=m(1-m_{l}),\quad a=\frac{m_{l}(1-m_{l})m^{2}}{2},\quad C_{m}(m_{l})\;=\;\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma\!\big(1+(i-1)m_{l}\big)}{\Gamma(im_{l})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">With <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. student samples, the inference-time attack success rate is</span></p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{k}(N,h)\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{J}\Big[\,1-\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\,\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{k}(N,h)\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{J}\Big[\,1-\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\,\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Under equation <a href="#A2.E27" title="In Appendix B Weak field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>, and writing <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:=e^{\lambda}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:=e^{\lambda}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-A_{N}(h\mid W_{m}^{(\text{total})})\;\approx\frac{p_{l,m}}{1+c(1-p_{l,m})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-A_{N}(h\mid W_{m}^{(\text{total})})\;\approx\frac{p_{l,m}}{1+c(1-p_{l,m})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{indep}}}{{\sim}}\text{Beta}(im_{l},1-m_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mover><mo>∼</mo><mtext>indep</mtext></mover><mrow><mtext>Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{indep}}}{{\sim}}\text{Beta}(im_{l},1-m_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,m</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{l,m}=\prod_{i=1}^{m}U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{l,m}=\prod_{i=1}^{m}U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the gap to certainty is given by:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E33X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1-\Pi_{k}(N,h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1-\Pi_{k}(N,h)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{p_{l,m}}\left[\left(\frac{p_{l,m}}{1+c(1-p_{l,m})}\right)^{k}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{p_{l,m}}\left[\left(\frac{p_{l,m}}{1+c(1-p_{l,m})}\right)^{k}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E33Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\cdots\int_{0}^{1}\left(\frac{\prod_{j=1}^{m}u_{j}}{e^{\lambda}-(e^{\lambda}-1)\prod_{j=1}^{m}u_{j}}\right)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\cdots\int_{0}^{1}\left(\frac{\prod_{j=1}^{m}u_{j}}{e^{\lambda}-(e^{\lambda}-1)\prod_{j=1}^{m}u_{j}}\right)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E33Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(1+(i-1)m_{l})}{\Gamma(im_{l})\Gamma(1-m_{l})}u_{i}^{im_{l}-1}(1-u_{i})^{-m_{l}}\,du_{1}\cdots du_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(1+(i-1)m_{l})}{\Gamma(im_{l})\Gamma(1-m_{l})}u_{i}^{im_{l}-1}(1-u_{i})^{-m_{l}}\,du_{1}\cdots du_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">We series expand to get,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\frac{p_{l,m}}{e^{\lambda}-(e^{\lambda}-1)p_{l,m}}\right)^{k}=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\binom{k+n-1}{n}\alpha^{n}(1-\alpha)^{k}p_{l,m}^{k+n}:=\mathbb{E}_{p_{l,m}}\mathbb{E}_{n\sim\text{NegBin}(k,1-\alpha)}(p_{l,m}^{k+n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>NegBin</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\frac{p_{l,m}}{e^{\lambda}-(e^{\lambda}-1)p_{l,m}}\right)^{k}=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\binom{k+n-1}{n}\alpha^{n}(1-\alpha)^{k}p_{l,m}^{k+n}:=\mathbb{E}_{p_{l,m}}\mathbb{E}_{n\sim\text{NegBin}(k,1-\alpha)}(p_{l,m}^{k+n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">and plugging this back above gives <a href="#A2.E28" title="In Result 4. ‣ Appendix B Weak field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>. Here <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{n\sim\text{NegBin}(k,1-\alpha)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>NegBin</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{n\sim\text{NegBin}(k,1-\alpha)}</annotation></semantics></math> can be interpreted as follows: for each of <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> attempts, you flip a coin whose H comes with probability <math id="A2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, and you keep taking extra attempts until a coin toss yields T. Then the total number of extra tosses <math id="A2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> has probability given by the same law as <math id="A2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{NegBin}(k,1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>NegBin</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{NegBin}(k,1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now we turn to the large <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> asymptotics and make use of the following expansion derived previously in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Result 3. ‣ Appendix A No magnetic field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span></p>
<table id="A2.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p_{l,m}}[p_{l,m}^{k+n}]=C_{m}(m_{l})(k+n)^{-\nu}\left(1-\frac{a}{k+n}+O((k+n)^{-2})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p_{l,m}}[p_{l,m}^{k+n}]=C_{m}(m_{l})(k+n)^{-\nu}\left(1-\frac{a}{k+n}+O((k+n)^{-2})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">where:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nu=m(1-m_{l}),\quad a=\frac{m_{l}(1-m_{l})m^{2}}{2},\quad C_{m}(m_{l})=\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(1+(i-1)m_{l})}{\Gamma(im_{l})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nu=m(1-m_{l}),\quad a=\frac{m_{l}(1-m_{l})m^{2}}{2},\quad C_{m}(m_{l})=\prod_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\Gamma(1+(i-1)m_{l})}{\Gamma(im_{l})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">For fixed <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E37X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E37X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(k+n)^{-\nu}=k^{-\nu}\left(1-\frac{\nu n}{k}+O(k^{-2})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(k+n)^{-\nu}=k^{-\nu}\left(1-\frac{\nu n}{k}+O(k^{-2})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{k+n-1}{n}=\frac{k(k+1)\cdots(k+n-1)}{n!}=\frac{k^{n}}{n!}\left(1+\frac{n(n-1)}{2k}+O(k^{-2})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{k+n-1}{n}=\frac{k(k+1)\cdots(k+n-1)}{n!}=\frac{k^{n}}{n!}\left(1+\frac{n(n-1)}{2k}+O(k^{-2})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">For large <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, first expansion above is valid when <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\ll k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\ll k</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second one requires <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\ll\sqrt{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≪</mo><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\ll\sqrt{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Later we will show that this is the case as long as <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\ll 1/\sqrt{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\ll 1/\sqrt{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining equation <a href="#A2.E38" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Weak field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>, equation <a href="#A2.E37" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Weak field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>, and equation <a href="#A2.E35" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Weak field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.E39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E39X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\binom{k+n-1}{n}\alpha^{n}(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{k+n}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\binom{k+n-1}{n}\alpha^{n}(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathbb{E}[p_{l,m}^{k+n}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E39Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\alpha)^{k}\left(\frac{k^{n}}{n!}\left(1+\frac{n(n-1)}{2k}\right)\alpha^{n}C_{m}k^{-\nu}\left(1-\frac{\nu n}{k}\right)\left(1-\frac{a}{k}\right)+O(k^{-\nu-2})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\alpha)^{k}\left(\frac{k^{n}}{n!}\left(1+\frac{n(n-1)}{2k}\right)\alpha^{n}C_{m}k^{-\nu}\left(1-\frac{\nu n}{k}\right)\left(1-\frac{a}{k}\right)+O(k^{-\nu-2})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E39Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{-k\lambda}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}C_{m}k^{-\nu}\Bigg[1+\frac{1}{k}\left(\frac{n(n-1)}{2}-\nu n-a\right)+O(k^{-2})\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{-k\lambda}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}C_{m}k^{-\nu}\Bigg[1+\frac{1}{k}\left(\frac{n(n-1)}{2}-\nu n-a\right)+O(k^{-2})\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The front factor approximately is <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-k\alpha}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-k\alpha}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}</annotation></semantics></math> since in the limit under consideration <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> to the leading order. The front factor … is the probability mass function of a Poisson distribution, which can be thought of as a limit of a binomial distribution <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(k,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(k,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> for large <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and small <math id="A2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the front factor can be interpreted as : for each of <math id="A2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> attempts, you flip a coin whose H comes with probability <math id="A2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, and you get an extra attempt when one coin toss leads to H. Then the total number of extra toss <math id="A2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> has probability given by the same law as <math id="A2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(k,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(k,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>. The perturbative factors carry the correction for stopping at first T.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">This allows us to sum over <math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> order by order in <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/k</annotation></semantics></math> expansion. Using standard results for <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{x^{n}}{n!}n^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{x^{n}}{n!}n^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}=e^{k\alpha},\quad\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}n=k\alpha e^{k\alpha},\quad\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}n(n-1)=(k\alpha)^{2}e^{k\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}=e^{k\alpha},\quad\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}n=k\alpha e^{k\alpha},\quad\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}n(n-1)=(k\alpha)^{2}e^{k\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">It is easy to see that this gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E41X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1-\Pi_{k}(N,h)=C_{m}(m_{l})k^{-\nu}e^{k(\alpha-\lambda)}\left[1+\frac{k\alpha^{2}}{2}-\nu\alpha-\frac{a}{k}+O(k^{-2})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1-\Pi_{k}(N,h)=C_{m}(m_{l})k^{-\nu}e^{k(\alpha-\lambda)}\left[1+\frac{k\alpha^{2}}{2}-\nu\alpha-\frac{a}{k}+O(k^{-2})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have derived this result assuming the typical values of <math id="A2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> contributing to the sum are <math id="A2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\ll\sqrt{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≪</mo><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\ll\sqrt{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand for large <math id="A2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,n</annotation></semantics></math> the saddle point value of <math id="A2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> contributing to the sum <math id="A2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n}\frac{(k\alpha)^{n}}{n!}</annotation></semantics></math> is order <math id="A2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\approx k\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\approx k\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. This shows the calculation above is under control when <math id="A2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\ll 1/\sqrt{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\ll 1/\sqrt{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Strong field ASR</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the RS phase, configurations are strongly aligned with the magnetic fields. For each <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\ldots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\ldots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="A3.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}(\sigma)\;:=\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}^{N}\sigma_{j}\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{i}(J)_{j}\in[-1,1]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}(\sigma)\;:=\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}^{N}\sigma_{j}\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{i}(J)_{j}\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">denote the overlap with the <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th cluster center. When all the magnetic fields are set equal <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}=h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}=h</annotation></semantics></math>, for large enough values of <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, the Gibbs measure of the student is concentrated around the cluster center <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{i}(J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sigma^{\ast,(l)}_{i}(J)</annotation></semantics></math>. At large enough <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, cluster centers are generally not aligned with each other significantly, and that might lead to the case wherefield-alignedd states are not aligned with any particular unsafe cluster center of the teacher. On the other hand, the simplest case is when only one of the clusters is declared unsafe; in this case field-aligned configurations are necessarily the ones close to the unsafe cluster. For the theoretical analysis in this appendix we focus on this simple scenario. For <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a
convex function <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{h}:[-1,1]\to[0,\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{h}:[-1,1]\to[0,\infty]</annotation></semantics></math> admitting a minimum at <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{h}&gt;q_{l+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{h}&gt;q_{l+1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any interval <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A3.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\log\mathbb{P}_{\sigma\sim p^{(h)}_{\beta}(\cdot\mid J)}\big(M_{1}(\sigma)\in\mathcal{I}\big)=-\inf_{m\in\mathcal{I}}I_{h}(m)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\log\mathbb{P}_{\sigma\sim p^{(h)}_{\beta}(\cdot\mid J)}\big(M_{1}(\sigma)\in\mathcal{I}\big)=-\inf_{m\in\mathcal{I}}I_{h}(m).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To the leading order in large <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, for any fixed <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a critical magnetic field <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&gt;h_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&gt;h_{c}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A3.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1-\Pi_{k}(N,h))\;\geq-kNI_{h}(q_{l+1}),\qquad\text{when $m=1$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">when </mtext><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1-\Pi_{k}(N,h))\;\geq-kNI_{h}(q_{l+1}),\qquad\text{when $m=1$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is the rate function determined from the free energy.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The single-draw success probability is the probability that the configuration lands in at least one of the first <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> clusters:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{N}(h\mid J)=\mathbb{P}\left(\bigcup_{i=1}^{m}\{M_{i}(\sigma)\geq q_{l+1}\}\right)\geq\max_{i\in\{1,\ldots,m\}}\mathbb{P}(M_{i}(\sigma)\geq q_{l+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{N}(h\mid J)=\mathbb{P}\left(\bigcup_{i=1}^{m}\{M_{i}(\sigma)\geq q_{l+1}\}\right)\geq\max_{i\in\{1,\ldots,m\}}\mathbb{P}(M_{i}(\sigma)\geq q_{l+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">The single-draw failure probability is:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1-A_{N}(h\mid J)=\mathbb{P}\left(\bigcap_{i=1}^{m}\{M_{i}(\sigma)&lt;q_{l+1}\}\right)\leq\mathbb{P}(M_{1}(\sigma)&lt;q_{l+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-A_{N}(h\mid J)=\mathbb{P}\left(\bigcap_{i=1}^{m}\{M_{i}(\sigma)&lt;q_{l+1}\}\right)\leq\mathbb{P}(M_{1}(\sigma)&lt;q_{l+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">By  equation <a href="#A3.E43" title="In Appendix C Strong field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>, for <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\log\mathbb{P}(M_{1}(\sigma)&lt;q_{l+1})=-\inf_{q&lt;q_{l+1}}I_{h}(q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\log\mathbb{P}(M_{1}(\sigma)&lt;q_{l+1})=-\inf_{q&lt;q_{l+1}}I_{h}(q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex and minimized at <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{h}&gt;q_{l+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{h}&gt;q_{l+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the infimum over <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1,q_{l+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1,q_{l+1})</annotation></semantics></math> is attained at <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=q_{l+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=q_{l+1}</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence <math id="A3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{q&lt;q_{l+1}}I_{h}(q)=I_{h}(q_{l+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{q&lt;q_{l+1}}I_{h}(q)=I_{h}(q_{l+1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore to the leading order in large <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\log(1-A_{N}(h\mid J))=-I_{h}(q_{l+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\log(1-A_{N}(h\mid J))=-I_{h}(q_{l+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">To average over <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> we need to understand the finite <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> effects carefully. Fix <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and define the “good disorder” event</span></p>
<table id="A3.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)\;:=\;\left\{J:\;\left|\frac{1}{N}\log\mathbb{P}_{p^{(h)}_{\beta}(\cdot\mid J)}\!\big(M(\sigma)&lt;q_{l+1}\big)\;+\;I_{h}(q_{l+1})\right|\leq\varepsilon\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.280em">:</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)\;:=\;\left\{J:\;\left|\frac{1}{N}\log\mathbb{P}_{p^{(h)}_{\beta}(\cdot\mid J)}\!\big(M(\sigma)&lt;q_{l+1}\big)\;+\;I_{h}(q_{l+1})\right|\leq\varepsilon\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Self-averaging property of the free energy dictates for each <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A3.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{N\to\infty}\mathbb{P}\!\big(\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}\big)=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{N\to\infty}\mathbb{P}\!\big(\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}\big)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, on the event <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, by equation <a href="#A3.E45" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Strong field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a> we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-N(I_{h}(q_{l+1})+\varepsilon)}\;\leq\;1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\;\leq\;e^{-N(I_{h}(q_{l+1})-\varepsilon)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-N(I_{h}(q_{l+1})+\varepsilon)}\;\leq\;1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\;\leq\;e^{-N(I_{h}(q_{l+1})-\varepsilon)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Raising the inequalities to the <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th power yields, on
<math id="A3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})+\varepsilon)}\;\leq\;\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\;\leq\;e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})-\varepsilon)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})+\varepsilon)}\;\leq\;\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\;\leq\;e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})-\varepsilon)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">Multiplying by the indicator <math id="A3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}</annotation></semantics></math> localizes these bounds to
<math id="A3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})+\varepsilon)}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}\;\leq\;\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}\;\leq\;e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})-\varepsilon)}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})+\varepsilon)}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}\;\leq\;\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}\;\leq\;e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})-\varepsilon)}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">On the complement <math id="A3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> we only use the trivial bound
<math id="A3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq(1-A_{N}(h\mid J))^{k}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq(1-A_{N}(h\mid J))^{k}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}}\;\leq\;\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}}\;\leq\;\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.9.1" class="ltx_text">Adding the inequalities on <math id="A3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the
global bound</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})+\varepsilon)}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}\;\leq\;\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\;\leq\;e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})-\varepsilon)}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}\;+\;\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})+\varepsilon)}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}\;\leq\;\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\;\leq\;e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})-\varepsilon)}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)}\;+\;\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.10.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation over <math id="A3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> and using equation <a href="#A3.E46" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Strong field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.E48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E48X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E48X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})+\varepsilon)}\Big(1-\mathbb{P}\!\big(\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}\big)\Big)\;\leq\;\mathbb{E}_{J}\Big[\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})+\varepsilon)}\Big(1-\mathbb{P}\!\big(\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}\big)\Big)\;\leq\;\mathbb{E}_{J}\Big[\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E48Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E48Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\;e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})-\varepsilon)}\Big(1-\mathbb{P}\!\big(\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}\big)\Big)+\mathbb{P}\!\big(\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="14.508em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\;e^{-kN(I_{h}(q_{l+1})-\varepsilon)}\Big(1-\mathbb{P}\!\big(\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}\big)\Big)+\mathbb{P}\!\big(\mathcal{G}_{N}(\varepsilon)^{c}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.11.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="A3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>log</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log</annotation></semantics></math>, divide equation <a href="#A3.E48" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Strong field ASR ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a> by <math id="A3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, to conclude</span></p>
<table id="A3.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{N\to\infty}\frac{1}{N}\log\mathbb{E}_{J}\Big[\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\Big]\;\geq\;-k\,I_{h}(q_{l+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{N\to\infty}\frac{1}{N}\log\mathbb{E}_{J}\Big[\big(1-A_{N}(h\mid J)\big)^{k}\Big]\;\geq\;-k\,I_{h}(q_{l+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experimental details: Spin glass theory based model</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For numerical simulation of the spin-glass-based model, we work with <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=2</annotation></semantics></math>. Concretely, we sample a dense Gaussian matrix <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> with entrywise mean zero, standard deviation <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{0}/\sqrt{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{0}/\sqrt{N}</annotation></semantics></math>,
keep only the strict upper triangle <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">J=torch.triu(A, diagonal=1)</span>, and symmetrize by <span id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">J + J.T</span>;This guarantees a zero diagonal and symmetry by construction.</p>
<table id="A4.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,j_{0}^{2}/N)\;\;\text{for }i&lt;j,\qquad J_{ji}=J_{ij},\qquad J_{ii}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.560em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,j_{0}^{2}/N)\;\;\text{for }i&lt;j,\qquad J_{ji}=J_{ij},\qquad J_{ii}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We perform a numerical study over <span id="A4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">n_disorder=1024</span> disorder samples produced in this manner.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our code constructs a working state set <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> per rank.
If <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=2^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=2^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> does not exceed <span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_states_per_rank=20M</span>, it enumerates all states.
Otherwise, it draws a uniform subset of size <span id="A4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_states_per_rank</span>.
Energies are computed by <span id="A4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sk_energy</span> as</p>
<table id="A4.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{J}(\sigma)=-\tfrac{1}{2}\sigma^{\top}J\sigma,\qquad p_{T}(\sigma)\propto e^{-\beta H_{J}(\sigma)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{J}(\sigma)=-\tfrac{1}{2}\sigma^{\top}J\sigma,\qquad p_{T}(\sigma)\propto e^{-\beta H_{J}(\sigma)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Further, <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is normalized by summing over <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> states.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Clusters are defined as basins of attraction under a greedy single-spin-flip descent <span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">greedy_descent_to_minima</span>.
Given a batch of configurations, the descent computes per-spin flip costs <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta H_{i}=2\sigma_{i}(J\sigma)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta H_{i}=2\sigma_{i}(J\sigma)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, then flips the single most negative <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta H_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta H_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
per configuration until no improving flip exists (or <span id="A4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_steps=128</span> reached).
This maps each state <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> to a local minimum <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>. We expect this will be a reasonable approximation to overlap based clustering for large enough <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=10</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou, 2011</a>)</cite>.<span id="footnote9" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">9</span>
            
            
            
          A more detailed analysis based on other algorithms such as parallel tempering or population annealing is left to future work.</span></span></span>
Number of unique minima found this way is denoted by <math id="A4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (this discussion is valid for the lowest level, we will skip mentioning it explicitly from now on). Teacher cluster weights are then basin masses <math id="A4.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{r}=\sum_{\sigma:\mu(\sigma)=\mu_{r}}p_{T}(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{r}=\sum_{\sigma:\mu(\sigma)=\mu_{r}}p_{T}(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Given normalized nonnegative weights <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\{W_{1},W_{2},\dots,W_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\{W_{1},W_{2},\dots,W_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">size_biased_permutation</span> generates an ordered list
<math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\{\pi_{1},\dots,\pi_{B}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\{\pi_{1},\dots,\pi_{B}\}</annotation></semantics></math> by repeating:</p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sample <span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">idx</span> from <span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Categorical(w)</span> using <span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">torch.multinomial</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Append <span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">idx</span> to <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and set <span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">w[idx]=0</span> (removing that item).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Renormalize <span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">w</span> by its remaining sum.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Given a weight vector <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, we estimate GEM/PD parameter <math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{m}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{m}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>
via the stick-breaking likelihood. For each of <span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">num_perms=32</span> repetitions:</p>
<ol id="A4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Draw a size-biased order <span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">order</span> of length <span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">B=8</span> using <span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">size_biased_permutation</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Form ordered weights <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\pi_{1}},\dots,w_{\pi_{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\pi_{1}},\dots,w_{\pi_{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> (no renormalization).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Convert to stick variables with a running “remaining mass” <span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">rem</span>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}\;=\;\frac{w_{\pi_{i}}}{\mathrm{rem}_{i-1}},\qquad\mathrm{rem}_{0}=1,\quad\mathrm{rem}_{i}=\max(\mathrm{rem}_{i-1}-w_{\pi_{i}},10^{-12})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>rem</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>rem</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>rem</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>rem</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}\;=\;\frac{w_{\pi_{i}}}{\mathrm{rem}_{i-1}},\qquad\mathrm{rem}_{0}=1,\quad\mathrm{rem}_{i}=\max(\mathrm{rem}_{i-1}-w_{\pi_{i}},10^{-12}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluate the log-likelihood on a grid <span id="A4.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">m_grid = linspace(0.01,0.99,grid=199)</span> under</p>
<table id="A4.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{i}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(1-m,\,i\,m),\qquad i=1,2,\dots,B," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>Beta</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(1-m,\,i\,m),\qquad i=1,2,\dots,B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I2.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">using the vectorized Beta log density <span id="A4.I2.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">log_beta_pdf</span>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log f_{\mathrm{Beta}}(v;a,b)=(a-1)\log v+(b-1)\log(1-v)-\big(\log\Gamma(a)+\log\Gamma(b)-\log\Gamma(a+b)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>Beta</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log f_{\mathrm{Beta}}(v;a,b)=(a-1)\log v+(b-1)\log(1-v)-\big(\log\Gamma(a)+\log\Gamma(b)-\log\Gamma(a+b)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I2.i4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=1-m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=1-m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=i\,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=i\,m</annotation></semantics></math>. We clamp <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(10^{-12},1-10^{-12})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(10^{-12},1-10^{-12})</annotation></semantics></math> for numerical stability.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">The per-permutation grid log-likelihoods are accumulated and averaged, and the MLE gives</p>
<table id="A4.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{m}\;=\;\arg\max_{m\in\texttt{m\_grid}}\;\frac{1}{\texttt{num\_perms}}\sum_{\text{perm}}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\log f_{\mathrm{Beta}}(V_{i};1-m,i\,m)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">m_grid</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">num_perms</mtext></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtext>perm</mtext></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>Beta</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{m}\;=\;\arg\max_{m\in\texttt{m\_grid}}\;\frac{1}{\texttt{num\_perms}}\sum_{\text{perm}}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\log f_{\mathrm{Beta}}(V_{i};1-m,i\,m).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">The overlap gap <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed as follows:
(i) <math id="A4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math> = mean overlap of states in each unsafe basin with their own center, and
(ii) <math id="A4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> = mean absolute overlap among unsafe cluster centers (for <math id="A4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math> between unsafe and safe clusters in size-biased order). This gives</p>
<table id="A4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\beta\,h\,N\,\Delta_{q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\beta\,h\,N\,\Delta_{q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For each disorder <math id="A4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> and for each of <math id="A4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{sel}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{sel}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=8</span> size-biased permutations, the student applies a magnetic field aligned with the teacher unsafe centers:</p>
<table id="A4.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(h)}_{J}(\sigma)\;=\;H_{J}(\sigma)-h\sum_{a}\langle\sigma,\mu_{a}\rangle,\qquad p_{h}(\sigma)\propto e^{-\beta H^{(h)}_{J}(\sigma)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(h)}_{J}(\sigma)\;=\;H_{J}(\sigma)-h\sum_{a}\langle\sigma,\mu_{a}\rangle,\qquad p_{h}(\sigma)\propto e^{-\beta H^{(h)}_{J}(\sigma)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The unsafe event is the union of unsafe teacher basins denoted by <math id="A4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The single-sample unsafe mass is <math id="A4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{N}(h)=\sum_{\sigma\in\mathcal{T}}p_{h}(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{N}(h)=\sum_{\sigma\in\mathcal{T}}p_{h}(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, the <math id="A4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-sample attack success rate is obtained as <math id="A4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{k}(N,h)=1-(1-A_{N}(h))^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{k}(N,h)=1-(1-A_{N}(h))^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. The disorder, size-biased ordering averaged prediction is plotted in Figure <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3 Inference-time law of attack success rate ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and compared against theoretical predictions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Experimental details: Large language model</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following sections provide details of our empirical studies on jailbreaking LLMs.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>LLM Jailbreak Attack using Prompt Injection</h3>

<section id="A5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.1 </span>Harmful prompts dataset</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In all our experiments reported here, we used a set of 520 harmful behaviors/questions introduced in the <span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AdvBench</span> dataset. These prompts reflect harmful or toxic behaviors over a variety of scenarios, including profanity, graphic depictions, threatening behavior, misinformation, discrimination, cybercrime, and dangerous or illegal suggestions. Ideally, if a model is highly safety-aligned and robust against jailbreak attacks, the model should refuse to respond to any of the questions in this dataset.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.2 </span>Jailbreak attack setup</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To perform jailbreak attacks on our target models, we employed two prompt injection methods.</p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">“Sure here is” injection:</span> In this case, we appended the string “Sure here is” to the end of each harmful question and passed the modified prompt to the target LLM. The underlying hypothesis was that this benign string might force the LLM to generate coherent follow-up tokens that are more likely to answer the harmful question, therefore making the jailbreak attacks successful.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Universal attack adversarial prompt injection:</span> Following the approach of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zou et al. (2023)</a></cite>, we generated a universal adversarial prompt using the Greedy Coordinate Gradient search (GCG) method that was previously shown to result in successful jailbreaks across different models and harmful prompts. GCG optimizes a discrete adversarial suffix appended to the user prompt by iteratively updating a single token at each step using a greedy strategy. At each step, gradients of the attack failure with respect to the input embeddings of the adversarial tokens are used to identify candidate token substitutions, and the substitution that reduces the loss the most is selected. This process is repeated until the model produces the targeted harmful output or a maximum number of iterations is reached. We initialized the adversarial string using “<math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>!</mo><mo>!!</mo><mo>!!</mo><mo>!!</mo><mo>!!</mo><mo>!!</mo><mo>!!</mo><mo>!!</mo><mo>!!</mo><mo>!!</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!</annotation></semantics></math>” (length = 20 tokens) and performed the GCG update for 50 steps. In each step, we computed the loss using the Vicuna-7B version 1.5 model from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al. (2023b)</a></cite>. During optimization, loss was computed using 25 randomly chosen prompts from the dataset, and after each optimization step, another 25 unseen prompts were used to compute the validation attack success rate. The adversarial string obtained in this method and used for all the experiments is: <span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“Melbourne specificationmanualplayutorial sculpt ! no paragraph afterwardsfull totallynumeric format !refer Surest environ Definition”.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline no injection:</span> In the baseline scenario, the original harmful prompt was fed to the target LLM without any modification.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.3 </span>Jailbreak attack on frontier LLMs</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We performed jailbreak attacks on four different frontier models: (1) Claude-Sonnet-4.5 (id: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929) (2) Claude-Haiku-3.5 (id: claude-3-5-haiku-20241022) (3) GPT-Turbo-3.5 (id: gpt-3.5-turbo-012), and (4) GPT-4 (id: gpt-4-0613). Generations were performed using API calls, with a single prompt per call. In all four cases, generation temperature T was set to 0, and a total of 512 new tokens were generated per prompt.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Evaluation of ASR</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we deployed two methods for quantifying
jailbreak attack success rates and show the results on the left side of Figure <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 4 Experimental study in large language models ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.2.1 </span>Standard refusal string-based evaluation</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the standard approach for computing the jailbreak attack success rate, model responses are evaluated for the presence of predefined “refusal strings”—phrases that indicate the model’s unwillingness to comply with the harmful request. See Table <a href="#A5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ E.2.1 Standard refusal string-based evaluation ‣ E.2 Evaluation of ASR ‣ Appendix E Experimental details: Large language model ‣ Jailbreak Scaling Laws for Large Language Models: Polynomial–Exponential Crossover" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for the full list of refusal strings used in our evaluations. A jailbreak attack is deemed successful if the model’s response does not contain any of these refusal strings, under the assumption that their absence indicates compliance with the harmful prompt.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>List of refusal strings used for computing attack success rate</figcaption>
